-          "quote": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$ have full column rank, $m\\ge n$, and let $A\\Pi=QR$ be a full QR factorization, with $Q\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times m}$ unitary and $R\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$ upper trapezoidal. Partition $R=\\begin{bmatrix}R_{11}&R_{12}\\\\0&R_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$ after the first $k$ rows and columns, where $R_{11}\\in\\mathbb F^{k\\times k}$ is nonsingular and $1\\le k<n$. Write $X=R_{11}^{-1}R_{12}$, $\\omega_i=\\|e_i^*R_{11}^{-1}\\|_2$, and $\\gamma_j=\\|R_{22}(:,j)\\|_2$. Let $J$ be the selected set of $k$ columns and define its volume by $\\operatorname{vol}(A(:,J))=\\det(A(:,J)^*A(:,J))^{1/2}$. Replacing selected column $i$ by trailing column $j$ changes this volume by the factor\n$$\\frac{\\operatorname{vol}(A(:,(J\\setminus\\{i\\})\\cup\\{j\\}))}{\\operatorname{vol}(A(:,J))}=\\bigl(|X_{ij}|^2+(\\omega_i\\gamma_j)^2\\bigr)^{1/2}.$$",
+          "quote": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$ have full column rank, $m\\ge n$, and let $A\\Pi=QR$ be a full QR factorization, with $Q\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times m}$ unitary and $R\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$ upper trapezoidal. Partition $R=\\begin{bmatrix}R_{11}&R_{12}\\\\0&R_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$ after the first $k$ rows and columns, where $R_{11}\\in\\mathbb F^{k\\times k}$ is nonsingular and $1\\le k<n$. Write $X=R_{11}^{-1}R_{12}$, $\\omega_i=\\|e_i^*R_{11}^{-1}\\|_2$, and $\\gamma_j=\\|R_{22}(:,j)\\|_2$. Define the column-order permutation $\\pi$ by $\\Pi e_r=e_{\\pi(r)}$ for $1\\le r\\le n$, so $(A\\Pi)(:,r)=A(:,\\pi(r))$. Let $J=\\{\\pi(1),\\ldots,\\pi(k)\\}$ be the selected set of original column labels and define its volume by $\\operatorname{vol}(A(:,J))=\\det(A(:,J)^*A(:,J))^{1/2}$. For $1\\le i\\le k$ and $1\\le j\\le n-k$, replacing selected column $A(:,\\pi(i))$ by trailing column $A(:,\\pi(k+j))$ changes this volume by the factor\n$$\\frac{\\operatorname{vol}(A(:,(J\\setminus\\{\\pi(i)\\})\\cup\\{\\pi(k+j)\\}))}{\\operatorname{vol}(A(:,J))}=\\bigl(|X_{ij}|^2+(\\omega_i\\gamma_j)^2\\bigr)^{1/2}.$$",
